{"parentUuid":"fed36e43-e5d4-4f2c-b0cf-a30a8651f52c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01EXuoRAVV3PDx2MRzsQicuN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# PR #1045 Review — Improve database credential redaction\n\n## What it does\n\n- Adds 4 new redaction layers on top of betterleaks: JDBC, DB URLs (`postgres|mysql|mongodb|...`), keyword DSNs (`REDACTED), semicolon/ODBC conn strings, plus bounded `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED form\n- JSON walker now key-aware: `seen` map keyed by `key+\\x00+val`, replacements scoped to value position via `replaceKeyedJSONValue`. Fixes value-collision over-redaction (e.g. `session_id` value matching another field)\n- Logging: kills `getLogger`/`getSessionID` snapshot helpers; `log()` holds RLock across `l.Log` so `Init`/`Close` can't close `logBufWriter` mid-write. Adds 8×log + 4×Init + 2×Close stress test\n- Drops `t.Parallel()` from 2 dispatch TUI tests that mutate package-level `newDispatchProgram`\n\n## Correctness\n\n**Solid**\n- Logger fix is the right scope. Comment \"do not shrink the lock scope to a snapshot pattern\" locks invariant. RLock allows concurrent loggers; only `Init`/`Close` serialize. ✅\n- Conn-string detectors properly gated: `hasKeywordDSNPassword` requires `host=` AND `user=` AND non-placeholder password before redacting the regex hit. Avoids prose FPs.\n- `hasDatabaseURLSecret` uses `url.Parse` + checks `password`/`pwd` query keys — reuses stdlib parser, scope-correct (userinfo URLs deferred to existing `credentialedURIPattern`, test confirms)\n- `replaceKeyedJSONValue` correctness: keyJSON is quoted (`\"password\"`), so substring collisions across keys can't happen. Mismatches advance `i = keyEnd`, no infinite loops. Verified value-position-only via `:` lookahead\n- `isCredentialJSONObject` (host+user siblings → credential context) prevents top-level `{\"password\":\"x\"}` from matching generic `password` key. Sensible gate\n\n**Minor concerns**\n\n- `credentialValuePattern` value group `[^\\s,;&]+` does not exclude `=`. `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED captures `foo=bar` as value. Probably fine (whole thing is secret) but inconsistent w/ shell semantics\n- `applyJSONReplacements` order: if r1 original is substring of r2 original, applying r1 first breaks r2 match. Low risk for full-string JSON values but no ordering doc\n- `isPlaceholderSecretValue` placeholder list (`xxx`, `xxxx`, `changeme`, `example`) is narrow. Real configs use `password`, `placeholder`, `REPLACE_ME`. Over-redaction of these is safer error, but call out\n- Dispatch TUI: removing `t.Parallel` is band-aid. Real fix is per-test factory injection or `t.Cleanup`. Acceptable as expedient\n\n## Performance\n\n`String()` now runs ~10 regex passes per call and is invoked per JSON value during JSONL redaction. Hot path for transcripts.\n\n- `detectConnectionStrings` short-circuits on no `=` — good\n- `detectCredentialValues` does NOT short-circuit. Add same `strings.ContainsRune(s, '=')` guard\n- No benchmarks added. Worth a micro-bench given transcript scale\n\n## Security\n\n- Always-on redaction expansion is correct privacy posture\n- `${VAR}` and `REDACTED`/`[redacted]`/`<redacted>` variants preserved → idempotent, won't double-redact\n- Userinfo URLs explicitly scoped out of new detectors (handled by existing layer) — clean separation, no double-firing\n- `Entire-Checkpoint`/transcript flow unaffected; redaction still pre-write\n\n## Test coverage\n\nStrong. 6 new test groups: DB conn strings, scope split (URL vs userinfo), bounded creds, over-redaction guards, structured JSON creds, normalized JSON keys (`\"DB Password\"`), value collision w/ skipped field. Race test uses real `Init`/`Close` cycles.\n\nGaps:\n- No bench for `String()` perf regression\n- No test for overlapping conn-string region merging (e.g. `jdbc:postgresql://...` matching both `jdbcPattern` AND `databaseURLPattern`) — relies on existing region merge logic\n- No test for very long transcripts (regex backtracking risk on `keywordDSNPattern` `(?:\\s+...)+{2,}`)\n\n## Conventions\n\n- Follows project privacy logging rules (no user content in logs)\n- Comment on `newDispatchProgram` flagging non-parallel constraint — good practice per CLAUDE.md `t.Parallel` rules\n- One stylistic nit: `connectionStringRules` is package-level mutable slice. Could be a `var = []connectionStringRule{...}` w/ explicit immutability comment, or unexported\n\n## Risk\n\nMedium. Always-on redaction change touches every transcript. Logger lock scope change touches every log call. Both are well-tested but blast radius is global. Recommend:\n\n1. Run `mise run test:e2e:canary` (per CLAUDE.md) to confirm Vogon doesn't trip on new redactions\n2. Spot-check perf on a representative transcript before merge\n\n## Verdict\n\nApprove with nits. Worth addressing before merge:\n\n- Add `=` short-circuit to `detectCredentialValues`\n- Add bench for `String()` to quantify regex stack cost\n- Consider splitting dispatch TUI commit (unrelated) into separate PR or noting in body"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18826,"cache_read_input_tokens":70689,"output_tokens":8873,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18826,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":8873,"cache_read_input_tokens":70689,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18826,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18826},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaVzshgtV9kSvyW3ycvE7","type":"assistant","uuid":"1ceb1c28-1e2f-4f32-a7a4-bc42023b21a3","timestamp":"2026-04-28T10:21:04.523Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate","sessionId":"754e21db-63c9-4876-b824-ee99608ee240"