s...)` call sites — keep their signatures; only package internals change.\n- Tests: `resetLogger()` mutates globals from `logger_test.go`. `TestLogging_ConcurrentInitAndLog` validates the race fix.\n- Settings dependency: `SetLogLevelGetter` callback (called 7 times before Init) — uses `context.TODO()`. May need rework.\n- Cobra entry: `main.go` calls `rootCmd.ExecuteContext(ctx)`. Commands receive `cmd.Context()`.\n\nRequirements:\n1. No package-level mutable state in `logging`. The `*slog.Logger` and any session/file state live in the context that flows from main.go.\n2. main.go opens the log file once and defers Close. Single ownership of file lifecycle.\n3. Hooks must still be able to attach session_id once they resolve it from disk in PreRunE, by enriching the ctx-logger and replacing the ctx.\n4. Existing context helpers (`WithSession`, `WithComponent`, etc.) should keep working — preferably by becoming thin wrappers over `logger.With(...)` + `WithLogger(ctx, child)`.\n5. The race from PR #1045 must remain impossible by construction. (Immutable logger in ctx; file closer only fires after main.go's defer = after all command goroutines complete.)\n6. Migration must be staged so each PR is independently reviewable and reversible. The 508 call sites should not all change at once.\n7. `objectsigner.go` `context.Background()` calls — propose how to thread real ctx in.\n\nDesign a detailed plan covering:\n- The new public API surface of the `logging` package (constructors, `WithLogger`, `LoggerFromContext`, fallback behavior, file Closer pattern)\n- How `log()`'s internals change (read logger from ctx, fall back to `slog.Default()`)\n- How `WithSession` / `WithComponent` etc. should be reimplemented to enrich the ctx-logger via `slog.With` instead of being read at log time\n- Concrete migration stages — which PR does what, what compiles / tests pass at each stage\n- Test strategy — how to replace `resetLogger()` and the concurrent test, what new tests are needed\n- Edge cases: settings log-level callback, pre-init logging (very early in main.go), test parallelism (no globals → tests can `t.Parallel()`)\n- Tradeoffs the user should know about (e.g., calling `logging.Info(context.Background(), ...)` falls back to stderr — is that acceptable?)\n- Files modified, with specific line ranges\n- A verification section: how to confirm the refactor is correct end-to-end\n\nAim for a plan that fits ~700 words. Be opinionated about the recommended approach."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6866,"cache_read_input_tokens":104103,"output_tokens":4487,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6866,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":4487,"cache_read_input_tokens":104103,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6866,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6866},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaW1VVUvWsDLRrZzaz3dk","type":"assistant","uuid":"ea74f185-aa8f-4bf0-bf22-07159117f6b2","timestamp":"2026-04-28T10:27:56.454Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate","sessionId":"754e21db-63c9-4876-b824-ee99608ee240","version":"2.1.119","gitBranch":"redact","slug":"i-do-think-that-parallel-metcalfe"}
{"parentUuid":"ea74f185-aa8f-4bf0-bf22-07159117f6b2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f754028b-255c-4616-97f5-a36084f8f0fa","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0162LjivzHYJrJ7QBnERKkaZ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Write tool isn't available — plan mode is read-only and I cannot create files. I'll deliver the plan directly as the response, per the system instructions (\"Do NOT Write report/summary/findings/analysis .md files. Return findings directly as your final assistant message\").\n\n---\n\n# Plan: Kill globals in `cmd/entire/cli/logging`\n\n## Recommended approach: logger-in-context with `slog.With` enrichment\n\nTreat `*slog.Logger` as an immutable value carried in `context.Context`. `WithSession`/`WithComponent`/etc. become `slog.With(...)` wrappers that produce a child logger and re-stash it in the ctx. `log()` reads the logger out of ctx (no locks). main.go owns the file. `attrsFromContext` is deleted — attrs are baked into the logger itself when each `With*` runs, so log-time extraction disappears.\n\nThis is simpler than a \"context-pulls-attrs-at-log-time\" approach: it eliminates `attrsFromContext`, drops `mu` entirely, and gives O(1) log calls with no per-call slice allocation.\n\n## New public API of `logging`\n\n```go\n// Constructor: opens log file, returns enriched logger + closer.\n// Closer flushes bufio.Writer and closes file. Idempotent.\ntype Closer func() error\nfunc Setup(ctx context.Context, opts Options) (*slog.Logger, Closer, error)\n\ntype Options struct {\n    SessionID string        // optional; baked in as slog attr\n    Level     slog.Level    // resolved by caller from env+settings\n    Output    io.Writer     // optional; defaults to file in <repo>/.entire/logs/entire.log, falls back to stderr\n}\n\n// Context wiring.\nfunc WithLogger(ctx context.Context, l *slog.Logger) context.Context\nfunc LoggerFromContext(ctx context.Context) *slog.Logger // never nil; falls back to slog.Default()\n\n// Existing helpers — reimplemented as slog.With + WithLogger.\nfunc WithSession(ctx, id) ctx       // l.With(\"session_id\", id) + parent_session_id promotion\nfunc WithParentSession(ctx, id) ctx\nfunc WithToolCall(ctx, id) ctx\nfunc WithComponent(ctx, name) ctx\nfunc WithAgent(ctx, name) ctx\n\n// Call sites unchanged — Info/Warn/Debug/Error/LogDuration keep current signatures.\n```\n\n`SetLogLevelGetter` is **removed**. Level resolution moves to a tiny helper `ResolveLevel(envValue, settingsValue string) slog.Level` called by main.go after it loads settings — no circular dep, no callback, no `context.TODO()`.\n\n## How `log()` changes\n\n```go\nfunc log(ctx context.Context, level slog.Level, msg string, attrs ...any) {\n    l := LoggerFromContext(ctx) // never nil\n    l.Log(ctx, level, msg, attrs...)\n}\n```\n\nNo mutex, no `attrsFromContext`, no nil-context dance. Attrs are already attached to `l` because `WithSession` etc. did `slog.With` upstream.\n\n## How `WithSession` etc. change\n\n```go\nfunc WithComponent(ctx context.Context, name string) context.Context {\n    l := LoggerFromContext(ctx).With(\"component\", name)\n    ctx = context.WithValue(ctx, componentKey, name) // keep getter API working\n    return WithLogger(ctx, l)\n}\n```\n\nEach helper does **two** things: bakes the attr into a child logger, and keeps the typed-key value in ctx so `ComponentFromContext` etc. still return strings to non-logging callers. `WithSession`'s parent-promotion logic stays.\n\n## Race safety by construction\n\n- Logger in ctx is immutable (`slog.With` returns a new logger).\n- File closer fires from main.go's `defer` after `ExecuteContext` returns. All command goroutines have joined by then, so no log call can race with `Close`. The PR #1045 lock guarding \"Init mid-write\" is unnecessary because there's no mid-flight Init anymore — `Setup` runs once.\n- Hook PreRunE enrichment only mutates the cobra `cmd.Context()` via `cmd.SetContext(ctx)`. It does not touch globals.\n\n## Migration stages (each PR compiles + tests green)\n\n**PR 1 — Add new API alongside old.** Add `Setup`, `WithLogger`, `LoggerFromContext`, `Closer`. Keep `Init`/`Close`/`SetLogLevelGetter` working untouched. Add unit tests for the new API. No call-site churn. Reversible: pure addition.\n\n**PR 2 — Wire main.go + root cmd.** main.go calls `logging.Setup` (with stderr-only output until repo root is known — see edge case below), gets `(logger, closer)`, calls `rootCmd.SetContext(logging.WithLogger(ctx, logger))`, defers `closer()`. Old `logging.Init` sites still run and overwrite the package logger; the ctx-logger is unused but inert. Reversible: revert main.go.\n\n**PR 3 — Convert `WithSession`/`WithComponent`/`WithToolCall`/`WithAgent`/`WithParentSession` to enrich the ctx-logger.** Now the 508 `logging.X(ctx, ...)` sites can already start picking up enriched ctx-loggers from PR 2. But because `log()` still reads the package-level `logger`, enrichment doesn't reach output yet. Reversible per file.\n\n**PR 4 — Flip `log()` to `LoggerFromContext`.** This is the load-bearing PR. From here on, the ctx-logger is authoritative. The package-level `logger` still exists but is unused at log time. Keep `Init` writing to it for one cycle to allow rollback. Run full test suite. Reversible: revert this single function.\n\n**PR 5 — Convert hook PreRunE.** `initHookLogging` returns `(ctx, Closer)`. PreRunE does `cmd.SetContext(ctx)`. PostRunE pulls the closer from a `cmd.Context()` value (or returns it from a small per-cmd struct attached via cobra's `Annotations`/closure capture — closure is cleanest). Delete `hookLogCleanup` global.\n\n**PR 6 — Convert per-command Init sites** (`attach`, `resume`, `clean`, `reset`, `rewind`, `explain`, `migrate`). Each replaces `logging.Init(ctx, \"\")` + `defer logging.Close()` with `ctx, closer, _ := logging.Setup(ctx, opts); defer closer(); cmd.SetContext(ctx)`. One file per PR if desired, or batch since they're independent.\n\n**PR 7 — Delete the corpse.** Remove `Init`, `Close`, `SetLogLevelGetter`, `mu`, `logger`, `logFile`, `logBufWriter`, `currentSessionID`, `resetLogger`, `attrsFromContext`. Update logger.go doc comment.\n\n**PR 8 — Fix `objectsigner.go`.** Thread ctx through `getCommitSigner`/`connectSSHAgent`. Their callers already have ctx (they're inside command flows). Caller chain: trace from each call site upward — all are reachable from cobra commands or hook handlers that have `ctx`. No `context.Background()` survives.\n\n## Test strategy\n\n- Delete `resetLogger()`. Replace with per-test construction: each test calls `logging.Setup(ctx, Options{Output: &buf, Level: slog.LevelDebug})` → gets a fresh logger in a local ctx. No global state, so tests can `t.Parallel()`.\n- `TestLogging_ConcurrentInitAndLog` becomes `TestLogging_ConcurrentLogToSharedLogger`: spawn N goroutines calling `logging.Info(ctx, ...)` against one shared ctx; assert no data race (run with `-race`) and that all N lines appear in the buffer. Init-mid-write is no longer a scenario — drop that branch.\n- New tests: `TestWithSession_BakesAttr` (assert `session_id` appears in output without `attrsFromContext`); `TestLoggerFromContext_FallbackToDefault`; `TestSetup_FileFallsBackToStderr` (unwritable dir); `TestWithSession_PromotesParent`; `TestEnrichmentChain` (Session→Component→ToolCall composes correctly).\n- Race regression: keep the test from PR #1045 but rewritten to exercise concurrent enrichment + logging through the same ctx.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- **Pre-Setup logging in main.go.** Before `Setup` returns, any log call uses `slog.Default()` (stderr text). Acceptable; main.go has nothing to log before `Setup` except signal-handler errors, which can use `fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, ...)` directly.\n- **Repo-root discovery.** `Setup` calls `paths.WorktreeRoot(ctx)`. If main.go is invoked outside a git repo (e.g. `entire --version`), fall back to stderr — same as today.\n- **Settings log-level callback.** main.go loads settings once after parsing flags but before dispatching to a subcommand's `RunE`. Pass the resolved level into `Options.Level`. Eliminates the `context.TODO()` in `config.go:78`.\n- **Test parallelism.** With no globals, every test is `t.Parallel()`-safe. Add `t.Parallel()` to all `logger_test.go` tests in PR 7.\n- **Cobra `SetContext` quirk.** `cmd.SetContext` replaces the ctx for that cmd and propagates to subcommands via `cmd.Context()`. Verified pattern; standard cobra idiom.\n\n## Tradeoffs\n\n- **`logging.Info(context.Background(), ...)` falls back to `slog.Default()` (stderr).** This is a behavior change: today such a call writes to the file via the global. Mitigation: `go vet` / a custom `analysis.Pass` to flag `context.Background()` arguments to `logging.*`, or just rely on PR 8 audit + grep. Acceptable — it surfaces bugs (the call site forgot to thread ctx) instead of hiding them.\n- **Enrichment cost is paid at `With` time, not log time.** If a hot path repeatedly enriches the same ctx, that's wasted allocation. In practice enrichment happens once per request boundary; logs in the loop reuse the already-enriched logger. Net win.\n- **Slightly larger ctx.** Each enriched ctx now carries a `*slog.Logger`. Negligible.\n- **Test isolation requires plumbing.** Tests that previously called `logging.Init` and asserted on the global must now thread their own ctx. Mechanical change; ~30 test sites estimated.\n\n## Files modified (with line ranges)\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go:44-63,65-72,74-141,143-159,161-175,256-331` — gut globals, rewrite `log`, delete `attrsFromContext`, delete `Init`/`Close`/`SetLogLevelGetter`/`resetLogger`. Add `Setup`/`WithLogger`/`LoggerFromContext`/`Closer`/`Options`/`ResolveLevel`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/logging/context.go:21-54` — rewrite each `With*` to do `slog.With` + `WithLogger` + keep typed key.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger_test.go:271,512,537,540-618` — drop `resetLogger`, rewrite concurrent test, add new tests, add `t.Parallel()`.\n- `cmd/entire/main.go:17-52` — call `logging.Setup`, attach to root ctx, defer closer, load settings + resolve level before dispatch.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go:64-86,87-89,108-120` — `initHookLogging` returns `(ctx, Closer)`; PostRunE consumes closer from closure (not global). Delete `hookLogCleanup` global.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/attach.go:80-84`, `resume.go:73-75`, `clean.go:76-78`, `reset.go:31-33`, `rewind.go:70-72`, `explain.go:267-269`, `migrate.go:52-56` — replace Init/Close with `Setup` + `cmd.SetContext`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/objectsigner.go:59,69` and surrounding signatures — thread ctx through `getCommitSigner`/`connectSSHAgent`/callers.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/config.go:78` — drop `context.TODO()`; level-loading happens in main.go now.\n\n## Verification (end-to-end)\n\n1. `grep -rn \"logging\\.\\(Init\\|Close\\|SetLogLevelGetter\\)\" cmd/entire` returns zero non-comment hits.\n2. `grep -rn \"var logger\\|var logFile\\|var logBufWriter\\|var currentSessionID\\|var mu \" cmd/entire/cli/logging` returns nothing.\n3. `grep -rn \"context\\.Background()\" cmd/entire/cli/objectsigner.go` returns zero.\n4. `go test -race -count=10 ./cmd/entire/cli/logging/...` clean.\n5. `go test -race ./...` clean.\n6. Manual: run `entire hooks git post-commit` in a test repo, tail `.entire/logs/entire.log`, confirm `session_id`, `component`, `agent` appear on every line and that `tool_call_id` appears only on tool-call lines.\n7. Manual: run `entire --version` outside a repo; confirm graceful stderr fallback, no panic, no `.entire/logs` created.\n8. Manual: `pkill -INT entire` mid-hook; confirm log file is closed cleanly (file end is a complete JSON line, not torn).\n9. Confirm `t.Parallel()` added to `logger_test.go` tests passes under `-race`.\n\n### Critical Files for Implementation\n- /Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go\n- /Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/cli/logging/context.go\n- /Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/main.go\n- /Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go\n- /Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/cli/objectsigner.go"}]}]},"uuid":"e8f0b4d3-c6f3-441b-ac12-dc9b6ab89dc7","timestamp":"2026-04-28T10:29:51.383Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Design a refactor of the `cmd/entire/cli/logging` package in this Go CLI repo. Goal: kill package-level globals (`logger`, `currentSessionID`, `logFile`, `logBufWriter`, `mu`) by initializing the logger once in `cmd/entire/main.go`, injecting it into the cobra root context, and enriching it with attrs (session_id, component, tool_call_id, agent) as the request flows.\n\nContext from exploration:\n- The package at `cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go` currently keeps `*slog.Logger`, `*os.File`, `*bufio.Writer`, `currentSessionID`, and a `sync.RWMutex` as package-level state.\n- `logger.go:260-289`: `log()` snapshots logger + sessionID under RLock and holds it across `l.Log(...)` (race-fix from PR #1045).\n- `logging/context.go`: already exposes `WithSession`, `SessionIDFromContext`, `WithParentSession`, `WithToolCall`, `WithComponent`, `WithAgent` and matching `FromContext` getters. `attrsFromContext` (in logger.go) extracts these and appends to every log line.\n- 11 `logging.Init(...)` sites: hook PreRunE in `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go:76`, plus per-command inits in `attach.go:80`, `resume.go:74`, `clean.go:77`, `reset.go:32`, `rewind.go:71`, `explain.go:268`, `migrate.go:53`. Hooks discover sessionID via `strategy.FindMostRecentSession(ctx)` in PreRunE; user commands pass `\"\"`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go:89,113,117-119`: a package-level `hookLogCleanup` var stores `logging.Close` for PostRunE — also smelly, kill it.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/objectsigner.go:59,69`: logs with `context.Background()` — depends on globals to materialize sessionID. Must be fixed by threading ctx down.\n- 508 `loggin