e dropped.\n\n## Approach\n\nTreat `*slog.Logger` as immutable value carried in `context.Context`. `WithSession`/`WithComponent`/`WithToolCall`/`WithAgent`/`WithParentSession` become thin wrappers: each does `LoggerFromContext(ctx).With(key, value)` then re-stashes the child logger via `WithLogger`. `log()` reads the logger from ctx (no locks). `attrsFromContext` is deleted — attrs are baked into the logger when each `With*` runs.\n\n`main.go` calls `Setup` once, gets `(*slog.Logger, Closer, error)`, attaches logger to ctx, defers closer. All commands/hooks receive the logger via `cmd.Context()`. Hooks that resolve sessionID at runtime call `ctx = WithSession(ctx, id); cmd.SetContext(ctx)` in `PersistentPreRunE`.\n\nSingle PR. No dual-path period. Aggressive deletion of obsolete code.\n\n## New `logging` package API\n\n```go\n// Constructor: opens log file, returns enriched logger + closer.\ntype Closer func() error\n\ntype Options struct {\n    Output io.Writer  // optional; defaults to .entire/logs/entire.log w/ 8KB buffer; falls back to stderr\n    Level  slog.Level // resolved by caller from env+settings\n}\n\nfunc Setup(ctx context.Context, opts Options) (*slog.Logger, Closer, error)\n\n// Context wiring.\nfunc WithLogger(ctx context.Context, l *slog.Logger) context.Context\nfunc LoggerFromContext(ctx context.Context) *slog.Logger // never nil; falls back to slog.Default()\n\n// Existing helpers — reimplemented as slog.With wrappers.\nfunc WithSession(ctx, id string) context.Context           // .With(\"session_id\", id) + parent promotion\nfunc WithParentSession(ctx, id string) context.Context     // .With(\"parent_session_id\", id)\nfunc WithToolCall(ctx, id string) context.Context          // .With(\"tool_call_id\", id)\nfunc WithComponent(ctx, name string) context.Context       // .With(\"component\", name)\nfunc WithAgent(ctx, name types.AgentName) context.Context  // .With(\"agent\", string(name))\n\n// Call sites unchanged — preserve current signatures of:\nfunc Debug(ctx, msg string, attrs ...any)\nfunc Info(ctx, msg string, attrs ...any)\nfunc Warn(ctx, msg string, attrs ...any)\nfunc Error(ctx, msg string, attrs ...any)\nfunc LogDuration(ctx, level, msg, start, attrs...)\n\n// Helper for level resolution (replaces SetLogLevelGetter callback).\nfunc ResolveLevel(envValue, settingsValue string) slog.Level\n```\n\n**Deleted:** `Init`, `Close`, `resetLogger`, `SetLogLevelGetter`, `getLogger`, `getSessionID`, `attrsFromContext`. Globals: `logger`, `currentSessionID`, `logFile`, `logBufWriter`, `mu`, `logLevelGetter`. Typed-key getters: `SessionIDFromContext`, `ParentSessionIDFromContext`, `ToolCallIDFromContext`, `ComponentFromContext`, `AgentFromContext` (no external readers).\n\n### `log()` after refactor\n\n```go\nfunc log(ctx context.Context, level slog.Level, msg string, attrs ...any) {\n    LoggerFromContext(ctx).Log(ctx, level, msg, attrs...)\n}\n```\n\nNo mutex. No `attrsFromContext`. Attrs already attached upstream via `slog.With`.\n\n### `WithSession` after refactor (representative)\n\n```go\nfunc WithSession(ctx context.Context, sessionID string) context.Context {\n    l := LoggerFromContext(ctx)\n    if existing := readAttr(l, \"session_id\"); existing != \"\" && existing != sessionID {\n        l = l.With(\"parent_session_id\", existing)\n    }\n    return WithLogger(ctx, l.With(\"session_id\", sessionID))\n}\n```\n\n(`readAttr` peeks at attached attrs via a tiny custom handler shim, OR — simpler — track parent session via a second context value. Recommend: keep one private context value `sessionIDKey` solely for the parent-promotion logic; do not export getters.)\n\n## Files modified\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go` | Gut globals + mutex. Rewrite `log()`. Delete `Init`/`Close`/`resetLogger`/`getLogger`/`getSessionID`/`attrsFromContext`/`SetLogLevelGetter`. Add `Setup`, `WithLogger`, `LoggerFromContext`, `Closer`, `Options`, `ResolveLevel`. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/logging/context.go` | Rewrite each `With*` to enrich ctx-logger via `slog.With`. Drop public `*FromContext` getters. Keep one private `sessionIDKey` only for parent-promotion. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger_test.go` | Drop `resetLogger` usage. Rewrite concurrent test as `TestLogging_ConcurrentLogToSharedLogger` (no Init mid-flight). Add `TestSetup_*`, `TestWithSession_BakesAttr`, `TestWithSession_PromotesParent`, `TestEnrichmentChain`, `TestLoggerFromContext_FallbackToDefault`. Add `t.Parallel()` everywhere (no globals → safe). |\n| `cmd/entire/main.go:17-52` | Call `logging.Setup(ctx, Options{Level: ResolveLevel(env, settingsLevel)})`, attach via `WithLogger`, defer `closer()`, pass to `rootCmd.ExecuteContext`. Resolve settings + level pre-dispatch. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go:60-89,97-121` | `initHookLogging` returns `(ctx, Closer)`. PreRunE: `ctx, closer := initHookLogging(cmd.Context()); cmd.SetContext(ctx)`. PostRunE: invoke closer captured in closure (not package var). Delete `hookLogCleanup` global. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/attach.go:80`, `resume.go:74`, `clean.go:77`, `reset.go:32`, `rewind.go:71`, `explain.go:268`, `migrate.go:53` | Replace `logging.Init(ctx, \"\")` + `defer logging.Close()` with: command pulls logger from `cmd.Context()` (already wired by main.go). For commands that need a session-scoped logger, wrap with `ctx = WithSession(ctx, sid); cmd.SetContext(ctx)`. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/objectsigner.go:59,69` | Thread `ctx` through `getCommitSigner` / `connectSSHAgent` callers. Replace `context.Background()` with the threaded ctx. Caller chain reachable from cobra commands — verify each before edit. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/config.go:78` | Drop `context.TODO()` + `SetLogLevelGetter` plumbing. Level resolution moves to main.go via `ResolveLevel`. |\n| Test files using `logging.Init`/`Close` (`checkpoint/committed_tripwire_test.go:30`, `checkpoint/v2_committed_tripwire_test.go:25`) | Replace with `ctx, _, _ := logging.Setup(ctx, Options{Output: io.Discard}); ctx = logging.WithLogger(ctx, logger)`. |\n\n## Reused functions / utilities\n\n- `slog.With` from stdlib — does the heavy lifting; no custom attr-merging code needed.\n- `paths.WorktreeRoot(ctx)` — `Setup` uses to find repo root for log file location (preserves current behavior).\n- `redact.JSONLContent` — unchanged; logging output already passes through redaction at write time via existing handler chain.\n\n## Migration order within the single PR\n\n1. Add new API (`Setup`, `WithLogger`, `LoggerFromContext`, `ResolveLevel`) without removing old. Compile.\n2. Wire main.go to `Setup` + `WithLogger`. Compile.\n3. Flip `log()` to read from ctx. Old `Init`/`Close` calls now no-op the global path; ctx-logger is authoritative.\n4. Convert `WithSession`/`WithComponent`/`WithToolCall`/`WithAgent`/`WithParentSession` to enrich the ctx-logger.\n5. Convert hook PreRunE/PostRunE to closure-captured closer.\n6. Convert per-command Init sites.\n7. Fix `objectsigner.go` ctx threading.\n8. Delete dead code: globals, `Init`, `Close`, `resetLogger`, `SetLogLevelGetter`, `attrsFromContext`, public `*FromContext` getters.\n9. Update tests: drop `resetLogger`, add `t.Parallel()` everywhere in `logger_test.go`, rewrite concurrent test, add new API tests.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- **Pre-Setup logging in main.go.** Before `Setup` returns, anything that logs uses `slog.Default()` (stderr). Acceptable — main.go has nothing to log before `Setup` except signal-handler noise, which uses `fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, ...)` already.\n- **Outside a git repo** (e.g. `entire --version`). `paths.WorktreeRoot` fails; `Setup` falls back to stderr. Same as today.\n- **`logging.Info(context.Background(), ...)` after refactor** silently goes to stderr because no logger is in `Background`. This is a behavior change — today such calls write to the file via the global. Mitigation: `objectsigner.go` is the known offender, fixed in step 7. Future leaks surface as missing log lines, not silent corruption — acceptable trade.\n- **Settings log level callback** (`SetLogLevelGetter`, called 7× before `Init`). Replaced by `ResolveLevel(env, settingsLevel)` invoked once in main.go after `settings.Load(ctx)`. No more `context.TODO()` in `config.go:78`.\n- **Test parallelism.** With no globals, `logger_test.go` tests gain `t.Parallel()`. Each test creates its own `(*slog.Logger, Closer)` via `Setup` writing to `&bytes.Buffer{}`.\n- **Cobra `cmd.SetContext`.** Replaces ctx for the cmd; subcommands inherit via `cmd.Context()`. Standard cobra idiom — verified in current `hooks_git_cmd.go` flow.\n- **Closer idempotency.** `Closer` must tolerate being called twice (defer in main.go + any explicit close). Implementation: guard with `sync.Once`.\n\n## Verification\n\n1. `grep -rn \"logging\\.\\(Init\\|Close\\|SetLogLevelGetter\\)\" cmd/ e2e/` → zero hits.\n2. `grep -n \"var logger\\|var logFile\\|var logBufWriter\\|var currentSessionID\\|var mu \" cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go` → empty.\n3. `grep -n \"context\\.Background()\" cmd/entire/cli/objectsigner.go` → empty.\n4. `grep -rn \"hookLogCleanup\" cmd/` → empty.\n5. `mise run check` passes (fmt + lint + test:ci).\n6. `go test -race -count=10 ./cmd/entire/cli/logging/...` clean — repeated to catch flaky races.\n7. `go test -race ./...` clean.\n8. `mise run test:e2e:canary` — full Vogon E2E suite passes (52 tests). Currently green per latest run, should remain green.\n9. Manual: run `entire hooks git post-commit` in a test repo, tail `.entire/logs/entire.log`, confirm `session_id`, `component`, `agent` appear on every line; `tool_call_id` only on tool-call lines.\n10. Manual: `entire --version` outside a repo — graceful stderr fallback, no `.entire/logs` created, no panic.\n11. Manual: `pkill -INT entire` mid-hook — log file ends on a complete JSON line (closer flushed via signal handler reaching main.go's defer).\n\n## Critical files\n\n- `/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go`\n- `/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/cli/logging/context.go`\n- `/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger_test.go`\n- `/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/main.go`\n- `/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go`\n- `/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/cli/objectsigner.go`\n- `/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/cli/config.go`\n- 7 per-command Init sites (`attach`, `resume`, `clean`, `reset`, `rewind`, `explain`, `migrate`)\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bbb705c8-e28b-49fd-9c43-0cd0d7f5a45c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate","sessionId":"754e21db-63c9-4876-b824-ee99608ee240","version":"2.1.119","gitBranch":"redact","slug":"i-do-think-that-parallel-metcalfe"}
