{"parentUuid":"f3a5d9c7-ab91-4de4-b9a5-80803fbbb0bb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01GJDanTL1Tg9di4VFzXX6Ps","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Roughly **5–7 more substantive branches** after this one. The big remaining ones:\n\n- (3) Where does log level resolution live (main.go vs `Setup` vs settings)?\n- (4) Closer plumbing through cobra (closure capture vs ctx-stored Closer vs cobra annotations)?\n- (5) `Setup` failure mode on file-open error (panic, error, or stderr fallback)?\n- (6) `objectsigner.go` ctx threading depth — how far up does it propagate?\n- (7) Behavior of `logging.X(context.Background(), ...)` after refactor — silent stderr or guardrail?\n- (8) Test convention enforcement (lint rule? doc-only? nothing?)\n\nPlus a handful of trivial naming/API-shape calls I'll batch at the end.\n\n---\n\nBack to **Question 2** — auto-promotion of `parent_session_id`. The grep shows it's exercised by 4+ tests and is the documented contract (`context.go:21-22`). Test `TestWithSession_SetsParentFromExisting` is a behavioral spec — promotion is load-bearing.\n\n**My recommendation: A.** Keep one private `sessionIDKey` context value purely for the promotion lookup. No public getter (`SessionIDFromContext` deleted — verified zero external callers). The slog logger is the only thing anyone *reads* attrs from; the ctx value is an internal detail of the `logging` package that exists solely so the next `WithSession` can compute the parent.\n\nConcrete:\n```go\nfunc WithSession(ctx context.Context, sessionID string) context.Context {\n    l := LoggerFromContext(ctx)\n    if existing, _ := ctx.Value(sessionIDKey).(string); existing != \"\" && existing != sessionID {\n        l = l.With(\"parent_session_id\", existing)\n    }\n    ctx = context.WithValue(ctx, sessionIDKey, sessionID)\n    return WithLogger(ctx, l.With(\"session_id\", sessionID))\n}\n```\n\nTrade: the package keeps one private context-value plumbed for one call site (promotion). Acceptable price for keeping current behavior.\n\n**A, B, or C?**"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2255,"cache_read_input_tokens":139895,"output_tokens":1270,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2255,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1270,"cache_read_input_tokens":139895,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2255,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2255},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaW51nZGKPmzqgCqr3462","type":"assistant","uuid":"45f98b42-5083-4d31-9af1-b00dac9bffbd","timestamp":"2026-04-28T11:13:20.788Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate","sessionId":"754e21db-63c9-4876-b824-ee99608ee240","version":"2.1.119","gitBranch":"redact","slug":"i-do-think-that-parallel-metcalfe"}
