{"parentUuid":"6cc044f6-cedd-4621-929a-51747944dff4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01337spuwsPep2iTaAdTuKbf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Question 8 — Test helper shape\n\nAfter the refactor, tests can't call `logging.Init`/`Close`. Each test that wants to assert on log output needs to: build a logger writing to a buffer, drop it in a ctx, exercise code, assert on the buffer.\n\nEstimated ~30 test sites need updating (`logger_test.go` ~20, `checkpoint/committed_tripwire_test.go`, `checkpoint/v2_committed_tripwire_test.go`, `integration_test/hook_logging_test.go`, plus any that use `resetLogger`).\n\nThree shapes for the test helper:\n\n**A. No helper. Each test builds its own:**\n```go\nvar buf bytes.Buffer\nl := slog.New(slog.NewJSONHandler(&buf, &slog.HandlerOptions{Level: slog.LevelDebug}))\nctx := logging.WithLogger(context.Background(), l)\n// exercise\n// assert on buf.String()\n```\n~5 lines per test. Clear, no magic. ~30 sites × 5 lines = 150 lines of boilerplate.\n\n**B. Public test helper in a `logging/loggingtest` subpackage:**\n```go\nctx, buf := loggingtest.New(t)  // returns ctx with logger writing to buf\n// exercise\n// assert on buf.String()\n```\nDRYs the boilerplate. Subpackage avoids polluting the main `logging` API. Pattern matches `httptest`, `testing/synctest`. ~30 sites × 1 line = clean.\n\n**C. Use `Setup` directly with `Options.Output: &buf`:**\n```go\nvar buf bytes.Buffer\nl, closer, _ := logging.Setup(context.Background(), logging.Options{Output: &buf, Level: slog.LevelDebug})\ndefer closer()\nctx := logging.WithLogger(context.Background(), l)\n```\nReuses the production constructor. Slightly more verbose than A. Tests exercise `Setup`'s lazy-writer path → catches bugs.\n\n**My recommendation: B (loggingtest subpackage).** Reasons:\n- 30 test migration sites is enough scale that DRY helps.\n- `loggingtest` matches Go stdlib conventions (`httptest`, `iotest`).\n- Helper can do useful extras: register cleanup, parse JSONL into structs for easier assertions, expose `WithSession`/`WithComponent` chainable shortcuts for common test setups.\n- Production `Setup` still gets exercised by integration tests + the canary E2E suite — no coverage loss.\n- Tests can `t.Parallel()` since each gets an independent buffer.\n\nConcrete API:\n```go\npackage loggingtest\n\n// New returns a ctx pre-loaded with a debug-level logger writing to buf.\n// Cleanup is registered on t.\nfunc New(t testing.TB) (context.Context, *bytes.Buffer)\n\n// NewWithLevel is like New but lets the test choose the level.\nfunc NewWithLevel(t testing.TB, level slog.Level) (context.Context, *bytes.Buffer)\n\n// Records parses each JSONL line in buf into a typed struct for assertions.\nfunc Records(t testing.TB, buf *bytes.Buffer) []Record\n\ntype Record struct {\n    Time    time.Time\n    Level   string\n    Msg     string\n    Attrs   map[string]any\n}\n```\n\nTrade vs A: tiny new public-test-API surface to maintain. Worth it for clarity at 30 sites.\n\n**A, B, or C?**"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1403,"cache_read_input_tokens":169899,"output_tokens":1989,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1403,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":1989,"cache_read_input_tokens":169899,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1403,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1403},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaWAGtgcr1uWryT16LGyH","type":"assistant","uuid":"48373af3-f912-4a92-9ab3-f3ad57237b28","timestamp":"2026-04-28T12:22:33.585Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate","sessionId":"754e21db-63c9-487