{"parentUuid":"7511cec4-df5f-4db4-be3b-a792ab7c2d58","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_014yoicGyjJQevjjN6cS2UMs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Question 9 — API shape (last substantive question, batched)\n\nFive small decisions left. I'll batch them and recommend defaults — confirm or override.\n\n### 9a. Constructor name: `Setup` or `New`?\n- `Setup` implies one-shot, side-effect-bearing init. Plan currently uses this.\n- `New` is Go's idiomatic factory verb. Returns value(s).\n- **Recommend: `New`.** Returns `(*slog.Logger, Closer)` — pure factory shape. `Setup` reads procedural; `New` reads functional. Aligns with `slog.New`.\n\n### 9b. Closer type: named `func` or `io.Closer`?\n- `type Closer func() error` — callable as `closer()`, idiomatic for \"deferred cleanup.\"\n- `io.Closer` interface — callable as `closer.Close()`, plays with stdlib helpers but slightly heavier syntax for callers.\n- **Recommend: named func.** main.go does `defer closer()`. Less typing, matches the \"single-shot cleanup\" semantic. We're not composing with stdlib `io.Closer` consumers.\n\n### 9c. `LoggerFromContext` fallback when no logger in ctx?\n- `slog.Default()` — stderr text. Quietest. Risk: hides \"I forgot to thread ctx\" bugs.\n- A no-op logger (writes go to `io.Discard`). Also quiet. Worse: total silence.\n- A package-level \"fallback logger\" that points to `os.Stderr` and emits a one-shot warning (\"logging: no logger in ctx, using fallback\") on first use.\n- **Recommend: `slog.Default()`.** Standard Go behavior, predictable, debuggable. The lint rule from Q7 covers the regression vector for `context.Background()`. One-shot warnings get noisy in tests — skip.\n\n### 9d. Keep `LogsDir` and `LogLevelEnvVar` exported?\n- Today both are exported (`logger.go:39,42`). External code may reference them (e.g., docs, error messages).\n- **Recommend: keep exported.** No reason to break callers. Both are stable strings.\n\n### 9e. `Options.Output` precedence when both `Output` is set AND a repo is detected?\n- Tests set `Output: &buf`; production leaves it nil and lets `New` lazy-open the repo path.\n- **Recommend: `Output != nil` wins, no lazy file logic engages.** Tests get deterministic in-memory output. Production sets `Output: nil` and gets the lazy path. Documented in `Options` struct doc-comment.\n\n---\n\n**Override any of these, or accept all five?** (Just say \"accept all\" or list the ones you want to change.)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1995,"cache_read_input_tokens":171302,"output_tokens":1264,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1995,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":1264,"cache_read_input_tokens":171302,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1995,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1995},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaWAY5Zst3cGqJh2Yh7L6","type":"assistant","uuid":"d79e766b-36b9-4a02-8b2d-110e749ec8e3","timestamp":"2026-04-28T12:25:46.201Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate","sessionId":"754e21db-63c9-4876-b824-ee99608ee240","version":"2.1.119","gitBranch":"redact","slug":"i-do-think-that-parallel-metcalfe"}
