t`. Each `With*` helper does `LoggerFromContext(ctx).With(key, value)` and re-stashes the child logger via `WithLogger`. `log()` reads the logger from ctx (no locks). `attrsFromContext` is deleted — attrs are baked into the logger when each `With*` runs.\n\nmain.go calls `New` exactly once, gets `(*slog.Logger, Closer)`, attaches the logger to ctx, defers the closer. **All commands and hooks receive the logger via `cmd.Context()` and only enrich it.** Per-command `Init`/`Close` calls and the hook `PostRunE` cleanup all delete entirely — there is one file, one Closer, one defer.\n\nThe log file (`.entire/logs/entire.log`, hardcoded) opens **lazily** on first write. Invocations that emit no logs (`entire --version` outside a repo) never create the file. First-write IO failure swaps the writer to `os.Stderr` and emits a one-shot stderr warning.\n\n## New `logging` package API\n\n```go\n// Constructor: returns logger + closer. No error — lazy writer handles IO failures internally.\ntype Closer func() error\n\ntype Options struct {\n    // Output, if non-nil, is used directly (tests set this to a *bytes.Buffer).\n    // If nil, New returns a logger backed by a lazy writer that opens\n    // .entire/logs/entire.log on first write, falling back to stderr on failure.\n    Output io.Writer\n    Level  slog.Level\n}\n\nfunc New(ctx context.Context, opts Options) (*slog.Logger, Closer)\n\n// Context wiring.\nfunc WithLogger(ctx context.Context, l *slog.Logger) context.Context\nfunc LoggerFromContext(ctx context.Context) *slog.Logger // never nil; falls back to slog.Default()\n\n// Existing helpers — reimplemented as slog.With wrappers.\nfunc WithSession(ctx, id string) context.Context           // .With(\"session_id\", id) + parent promotion\nfunc WithParentSession(ctx, id string) context.Context     // .With(\"parent_session_id\", id)\nfunc WithToolCall(ctx, id string) context.Context          // .With(\"tool_call_id\", id)\nfunc WithComponent(ctx, name string) context.Context       // .With(\"component\", name)\nfunc WithAgent(ctx, name types.AgentName) context.Context  // .With(\"agent\", string(name))\n\n// Pure helper for level precedence (env wins, then settings, then info default).\nfunc ResolveLevel(envValue, settingsValue string) slog.Level\n\n// Call sites unchanged.\nfunc Debug(ctx, msg string, attrs ...any)\nfunc Info(ctx, msg string, attrs ...any)\nfunc Warn(ctx, msg string, attrs ...any)\nfunc Error(ctx, msg string, attrs ...any)\nfunc LogDuration(ctx, level, msg string, start time.Time, attrs ...any)\n\n// Kept exported (zero churn cost):\nconst LogsDir       = \".entire/logs\"\nconst LogLevelEnvVar = \"ENTIRE_LOG_LEVEL\"\n```\n\n**Deleted:** `Init`, `Close`, `resetLogger`, `SetLogLevelGetter`, `getLogger`, `getSessionID`, `attrsFromContext`. Globals: `logger`, `currentSessionID`, `logFile`, `logBufWriter`, `mu`, `logLevelGetter`. Public typed-key getters: `SessionIDFromContext`, `ParentSessionIDFromContext`, `ToolCallIDFromContext`, `ComponentFromContext`, `AgentFromContext` (no external readers — verified).\n\n### `log()` after refactor\n\n```go\nfunc log(ctx context.Context, level slog.Level, msg string, attrs ...any) {\n    LoggerFromContext(ctx).Log(ctx, level, msg, attrs...)\n}\n```\n\nNo mutex. No `attrsFromContext`. Attrs are already attached upstream via `slog.With`.\n\n### `WithSession` after refactor (parent-promotion preserved)\n\nThe package keeps **one private** context value `sessionIDKey` solely so the next `WithSession` can compute the parent. No public getter exposed.\n\n```go\ntype ctxKey int\nconst sessionIDKey ctxKey = iota // private; only used inside this package\n\nfunc WithSession(ctx context.Context, sessionID string) context.Context {\n    l := LoggerFromContext(ctx)\n    if existing, _ := ctx.Value(sessionIDKey).(string); existing != \"\" && existing != sessionID {\n        l = l.With(\"parent_session_id\", existing)\n    }\n    ctx = context.WithValue(ctx, sessionIDKey, sessionID)\n    return WithLogger(ctx, l.With(\"session_id\", sessionID))\n}\n```\n\n### Lazy writer (file lifecycle)\n\n```go\n// Internal type; not exported.\ntype lazyWriter struct {\n    once     sync.Once       // guards open\n    closeOnce sync.Once      // guards close — Closer is idempotent\n    target   io.Writer       // set by once: file (with bufio) or os.Stderr\n    closer   func() error    // set by once: file flush+close, or no-op\n}\n\nfunc (w *lazyWriter) Write(p []byte) (int, error) {\n    w.once.Do(func() {\n        // attempt to open .entire/logs/entire.log relative to paths.WorktreeRoot(ctx).\n        // on failure: print a one-shot warning to os.Stderr; set target=os.Stderr.\n    })\n    return w.target.Write(p)\n}\n```\n\nCloser is `sync.Once`-guarded — safe to invoke multiple times (e.g., main.go's defer + any test harness double-close).\n\n## Files modified\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go` | Gut globals + mutex. Rewrite `log()`. Delete `Init`/`Close`/`resetLogger`/`getLogger`/`getSessionID`/`attrsFromContext`/`SetLogLevelGetter`. Add `New`, `WithLogger`, `LoggerFromContext`, `Closer`, `Options`, `ResolveLevel`, internal `lazyWriter`. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/logging/context.go` | Rewrite each `With*` to enrich the ctx-logger via `slog.With` + `WithLogger`. Drop public `*FromContext` getters. Keep one private `sessionIDKey` for parent-promotion only. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger_test.go` | Drop `resetLogger` usage. Rewrite concurrent test as `TestLogging_ConcurrentLogToSharedLogger`. Add new tests (see Test Strategy). Add `t.Parallel()` to every test. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/logging/loggingtest/loggingtest.go` (NEW) | Test helper subpackage: `New(t)` returns `(ctx, *bytes.Buffer)`; `NewWithLevel`; `Records(t, buf) []Record`. |\n| `cmd/entire/main.go:17-52` | Load settings (graceful failure outside repo). Compute `level := logging.ResolveLevel(os.Getenv(logging.LogLevelEnvVar), s.LogLevel)`. Call `logger, closer := logging.New(ctx