ionID`, `*os.File`, `*bufio.Writer`, and a `sync.RWMutex` as package-level mutable state. PR #1045 added `TestLogging_ConcurrentInitAndLog` and widened the lock scope in `log()` because `Init`/`Close` could close `logBufWriter` mid-write — a symptom of mutable shared state."," ","-The package already has context helpers (`WithSession`, `WithComponent`, `WithToolCall`, `WithAgent`, `WithParentSession`) and `attrsFromContext` that pull attrs out at log time. Sessions, components, etc. already flow through `context.Context` — only the `*slog.Logger` itself and `sessionID` are still globals, and only `currentSessionID` is the load-bearing duplicate (it's also pulled from ctx via `WithSession`, but the global takes precedence at log time per `logger.go:302`).","+Goal: init the logger once in `cmd/entire/main.go`, inject it into the cobra root context, enrich it via `slog.With(...)` as the request flows. Eliminate every package-level mutable. The race from PR #1045 disappears by construction (logger value in ctx is immutable; file closer fires after `ExecuteContext` returns)."," ","-Goal: init once in `main.go`, inject `*slog.Logger` into the cobra root context, enrich via `slog.With(...)` as the request flows. Eliminate every package-level mutable. Race from PR #1045 disappears by construction (logger value in ctx is immutable; file closer fires after `ExecuteContext` returns).","+The `logging/context.go` package already exposes `WithSession`/`WithComponent`/`WithToolCall`/`WithAgent`/`WithParentSession` — the *attrs* already flow through ctx, only the `*slog.Logger` itself plus `currentSessionID` are still globals. No external package reads `*FromContext` getters (verified). The dead file `cmd/entire/cli/objectsigner.go` (superseded by `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go`) gets cleaned up while we're in the area."," ","-No external callers read `SessionIDFromContext`/`ComponentFromContext`/etc. (verified via grep) — typed-key getters can be dropped.","+Single PR. No dual-path period. Aggressive deletion of obsolete code."," "," ## Approach"," ","-Treat `*slog.Logger` as immutable value carried in `context.Context`. `WithSession`/`WithComponent`/`WithToolCall`/`WithAgent`/`WithParentSession` become thin wrappers: each does `LoggerFromContext(ctx).With(key, value)` then re-stashes the child logger via `WithLogger`. `log()` reads the logger from ctx (no locks). `attrsFromContext` is deleted — attrs are baked into the logger when each `With*` runs.","+Treat `*slog.Logger` as immutable value carried in `context.Context`. Each `With*` helper does `LoggerFromContext(ctx).With(key, value)` and re-stashes the child logger via `WithLogger`. `log()` reads the logger from ctx (no locks). `attrsFromContext` is deleted — attrs are baked into the logger when each `With*` runs."," ","-`main.go` calls `Setup` once, gets `(*slog.Logger, Closer, error)`, attaches logger to ctx, defers closer. All commands/hooks receive the logger via `cmd.Context()`. Hooks that resolve sessionID at runtime call `ctx = WithSession(ctx, id); cmd.SetContext(ctx)` in `PersistentPreRunE`.","+main.go calls `New` exactly once, gets `(*slog.Logger, Closer)`, attaches the logger to ctx, defers the closer. **All commands and hooks receive the logger via `cmd.Context()` and only enrich it.** Per-command `Init`/`Close` calls and the hook `PostRunE` cleanup all delete entirely — there is one file, one Closer, one defer."," ","-Single PR. No dual-path period. Aggressive deletion of obsolete code.","+The log file (`.entire/logs/entire.log`, hardcoded) opens **lazily** on first write. Invocations that emit no logs (`entire --version` outside a repo) never create the file. First-write IO failure swaps the writer to `os.Stderr` and emits a one-shot stderr warning."," "," ## New `logging` package API"," "," ```go","-// Constructor: opens log file, returns enriched logger + closer.","+// Constructor: returns logger + closer. No error — lazy writer handles IO failures internally."," type Closer func() error"," "," type Options struct {","-    Output io.Writer  // optional; defaults to .entire/logs/entire.log w/ 8KB buffer; falls back to stderr","-    Level  slog.Level // resolved by caller from env+settings","+    // Output, if non-nil, is used directly (tests set this to a *bytes.Buffer).","+    // If nil, New returns a logger backed by a lazy writer that opens","+    // .entire/logs/entire.log on first write, falling back to stderr on failure.","+    Output io.Writer","+    Level  slog.Level"," }"," ","-func Setup(ctx context.Context, opts Options) (*slog.Logger, Closer, error)","+func New(ctx context.Context, opts Options) (*slog.Logger, Closer)"," "," // Context wiring."," func WithLogger(ctx context.Context, l *slog.Logger) context.Context"]},{"oldStart":42,"oldLines":18,"newStart":45,"newLines":22,"lines":[" func WithComponent(ctx, name string) context.Context       // .With(\"component\", name)"," func WithAgent(ctx, name types.AgentName) context.Context  // .With(\"agent\", string(name))"," ","-// Call sites unchanged — preserve current signatures of:","+// Pure helper for level precedence (env wins, then settings, then info default).","+func ResolveLevel(envValue, settingsValue string) slog.Level","+","+// Call sites unchanged."," func Debug(ctx, msg string, attrs ...any)"," func Info(ctx, msg string, attrs ...any)"," func Warn(ctx, msg string, attrs ...any)"," func Error(ctx, msg string, attrs ...any)","-func LogDuration(ctx, level, msg, start, attrs...)","+func LogDuration(ctx, level, msg string, start time.Time, attrs ...any)"," ","-// Helper for level resolution (replaces SetLogLevelGetter callback).","-func ResolveLevel(envValue, settingsValue string) slog.Level","+// Kept exported (zero churn cost):","+const LogsDir       = \".entire/logs\"","+const LogLevelEnvVar = \"ENTIRE_LOG_LEVEL\""," ```"," ","-**Deleted:** `Init`, `Close`, `resetLogger`, `SetLogLevelGetter`, `getLogger`, `getSessionID`, `attrsFromContext`. Globals: `logger`, `currentSessionID`, `logFile`, `logBufWriter`, `mu`, `logLevelGetter`. Typed-key getters: `SessionIDFromContext`, `ParentSessionIDFromContext`, `ToolCallIDFromContext`, `ComponentFromContext`, `AgentFromContext` (no external readers).","+**Deleted:** `Init`, `Close`, `resetLogger`, `SetLogLevelGetter`, `getLogger`, `getSessionID`, `attrsFromContext`. Globals: `logger`, `currentSessionID`, `logFile`, `logBufWriter`, `mu`, `logLevelGetter`. Public typed-key getters: `SessionIDFromContext`, `ParentSessionIDFromContext`, `ToolCallIDFromContext`, `ComponentFromContext`, `AgentFromContext` (no external readers — verified)."," "," ### `log()` after refactor"," "]},{"oldStart":63,"oldLines":85,"newStart":70,"newLines":167,"lines":[" }"," ```"," ","-No mutex. No `attrsFromContext`. Attrs already attached upstream via `slog.With`.","+No mutex. No `attrsFromContext`. Attrs are already attached upstream via `slog.With`."," ","-### `WithSession` after refactor (representative)","+### `WithSession` after refactor (parent-promotion preserved)"," ","+The package keeps **one private** context value `sessionIDKey` solely so the next `WithSession` can compute the parent. No public getter exposed.","+"," ```go","+type ctxKey int","+const sessionIDKey ctxKey = iota // private; only used inside this package","+"," func WithSession(ctx context.Context, sessionID string) context.Context {","     l := LoggerFromContext(ctx)","-    if existing := readAttr(l, \"session_id\"); existing != \"\" && existing != sessionID {","+    if existing, _ := ctx.Value(sessionIDKey).(string); existing != \"\" && existing != sessionID {","         l = l.With(\"parent_session_id\", existing)","     }","+    ctx = context.WithValue(ctx, sessionIDKey, sessionID)","     return WithLogger(ctx, l.With(\"session_id\", sessionID))"," }"," ```"," ","-(`readAttr` peeks at attached attrs via a tiny custom handler shim, OR — simpler — track parent session via a second context value. Recommend: keep one private context value `sessionIDKey` solely for the parent-promotion logic; do not export getters.)","+### Lazy writer (file lifecycle)"," ","+```go","+// Internal type; not exported.","+type lazyWriter struct {","+    once     sync.Once       // guards open","+    closeOnce sync.Once      // guards close — Closer is idempotent","+    target   io.Writer       // set by once: file (with bufio) or os.Stderr","+    closer   func() error    // set by once: file flush+close, or no-op","+}","+","+func (w *lazyWriter) Write(p []byte) (int, error) {","+    w.once.Do(func() {","+        // attempt to open .entire/logs/entire.log relative to paths.WorktreeRoot(ctx).","+        // on failure: print a one-shot warning to os.Stderr; set target=os.Stderr.","+    })","+    return w.target.Write(p)","+}","+```","+","+Closer is `sync.Once`-guarded — safe to invoke multiple times (e.g., main.go's defer + any test harness double-close).","+"," ## Files modified"," "," | File | Change |"," |---|---|","-| `cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go` | Gut globals + mutex. Rewrite `log()`. Delete `Init`/`Close`/`resetLogger`/`getLogger`/`getSessionID`/`attrsFromContext`/`SetLogLevelGetter`. Add `Setup`, `WithLogger`, `LoggerFromContext`, `Closer`, `Options`, `ResolveLevel`. |","-| `cmd/entire/cli/logging/context.go` | Rewrite each `With*` to enrich ctx-logger via `slog.With`. Drop public `*FromContext` getters. Keep one private `sessionIDKey` only for parent-promotion. |","-| `cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger_test.go` | Drop `resetLogger` usage. Rewrite concurrent test as `TestLogging_ConcurrentLogToSharedLogger` (no Init mid-flight). Add `TestSetup_*`, `TestWithSession_BakesAttr`, `TestWithSession_PromotesParent`, `TestEnrichmentChain`, `TestLoggerFromContext_FallbackToDefault`. Add `t.Parallel()` everywhere (no globals → safe). |","-| `cmd/entire/main.go:17-52` | Call `logging.Setup(ctx, Options{Level: ResolveLevel(env, settingsLevel)})`, attach via `WithLogger`, defer `closer()`, pass to `rootCmd.ExecuteContext