x (no locks). `attrsFromContext` is deleted — attrs are baked into the logger when each `With*` runs.\n\nmain.go calls `New` exactly once, gets `(*slog.Logger, Closer)`, attaches the logger to ctx, defers the closer. **All commands and hooks receive the logger via `cmd.Context()` and only enrich it.** Per-command `Init`/`Close` calls and the hook `PostRunE` cleanup all delete entirely — there is one file, one Closer, one defer.\n\nThe log file (`.entire/logs/entire.log`, hardcoded) opens **lazily** on first write. Invocations that emit no logs (`entire --version` outside a repo) never create the file. First-write IO failure swaps the writer to `os.Stderr` and emits a one-shot stderr warning.\n\n## New `logging` package API\n\n```go\n// Constructor: returns logger + closer. No error — lazy writer handles IO failures internally.\ntype Closer func() error\n\ntype Options struct {\n    // Output, if non-nil, is used directly (tests set this to a *bytes.Buffer).\n    // If nil, New returns a logger backed by a lazy writer that opens\n    // .entire/logs/entire.log on first write, falling back to stderr on failure.\n    Output io.Writer\n    Level  slog.Level\n}\n\nfunc New(ctx context.Context, opts Options) (*slog.Logger, Closer)\n\n// Context wiring.\nfunc WithLogger(ctx context.Context, l *slog.Logger) context.Context\nfunc LoggerFromContext(ctx context.Context) *slog.Logger // never nil; falls back to slog.Default()\n\n// Existing helpers — reimplemented as slog.With wrappers.\nfunc WithSession(ctx, id string) context.Context           // .With(\"session_id\", id) + parent promotion\nfunc WithParentSession(ctx, id string) context.Context     // .With(\"parent_session_id\", id)\nfunc WithToolCall(ctx, id string) context.Context          // .With(\"tool_call_id\", id)\nfunc WithComponent(ctx, name string) context.Context       // .With(\"component\", name)\nfunc WithAgent(ctx, name types.AgentName) context.Context  // .With(\"agent\", string(name))\n\n// Pure helper for level precedence (env wins, then settings, then info default).\nfunc ResolveLevel(envValue, settingsValue string) slog.Level\n\n// Call sites unchanged.\nfunc Debug(ctx, msg string, attrs ...any)\nfunc Info(ctx, msg string, attrs ...any)\nfunc Warn(ctx, msg string, attrs ...any)\nfunc Error(ctx, msg string, attrs ...any)\nfunc LogDuration(ctx, level, msg string, start time.Time, attrs ...any)\n\n// Kept exported (zero churn cost):\nconst LogsDir       = \".entire/logs\"\nconst LogLevelEnvVar = \"ENTIRE_LOG_LEVEL\"\n```\n\n**Deleted:** `Init`, `Close`, `resetLogger`, `SetLogLevelGetter`, `getLogger`, `getSessionID`, `attrsFromContext`. Globals: `logger`, `currentSessionID`, `logFile`, `logBufWriter`, `mu`, `logLevelGetter`. Public typed-key getters: `SessionIDFromContext`, `ParentSessionIDFromContext`, `ToolCallIDFromContext`, `ComponentFromContext`, `AgentFromContext` (no external readers — verified).\n\n### `log()` after refactor\n\n```go\nfunc log(ctx context.Context, level slog.Level, msg string, attrs ...any) {\n    LoggerFromContext(ctx).Log(ctx, level, msg, attrs...)\n}\n```\n\nNo mutex. No `attrsFromContext`. Attrs are already attached upstream via `slog.With`.\n\n### `WithSession` after refactor (parent-promotion preserved)\n\nThe package keeps **one private** context value `sessionIDKey` solely so the next `WithSession` can compute the parent. No public getter exposed.\n\n```go\ntype ctxKey int\nconst sessionIDKey ctxKey = iota // private; only used inside this package\n\nfunc WithSession(ctx context.Context, sessionID string) context.Context {\n    l := LoggerFromContext(ctx)\n    if existing, _ := ctx.Value(sessionIDKey).(string); existing != \"\" && existing != sessionID {\n        l = l.With(\"parent_session_id\", existing)\n    }\n    ctx = context.WithValue(ctx, sessionIDKey, sessionID)\n    return WithLogger(ctx, l.With(\"session_id\", sessionID))\n}\n```\n\n### Lazy writer (file lifecycle)\n\n```go\n// Internal type; not exported.\ntype lazyWriter struct {\n    once     sync.Once       // guards open\n    closeOnce sync.Once      // guards close — Closer is idempotent\n    target   io.Writer       // set by once: file (with bufio) or os.Stderr\n    closer   func() error    // set by once: file flush+close, or no-op\n}\n\nfunc (w *lazyWriter) Write(p []byte) (int, error) {\n    w.once.Do(func() {\n        // attempt to open .entire/logs/entire.log relative to paths.WorktreeRoot(ctx).\n        // on failure: print a one-shot warning to os.Stderr; set target=os.Stderr.\n    })\n    return w.target.Write(p)\n}\n```\n\nCloser is `sync.Once`-guarded — safe to invoke multiple times (e.g., main.go's defer + any test harness double-close).\n\n## Files modified\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go` | Gut globals + mutex. Rewrite `log()`. Delete `Init`/`Close`/`resetLogger`/`getLogger`/`getSessionID`/`attrsFromContext`/`SetLogLevelGetter`. Add `New`, `WithLogger`, `LoggerFromContext`, `Closer`, `Options`, `ResolveLevel`, internal `lazyWriter`. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/logging/context.go` | Rewrite each `With*` to enrich the ctx-logger via `slog.With` + `WithLogger`. Drop public `*FromContext` getters. Keep one private `sessionIDKey` for parent-promotion only. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger_test.go` | Drop `resetLogger` usage. Rewrite concurrent test as `TestLogging_ConcurrentLogToSharedLogger`. Add new tests (see Test Strategy). Add `t.Parallel()` to every test. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/logging/loggingtest/loggingtest.go` (NEW) | Test helper subpackage: `New(t)` returns `(ctx, *bytes.Buffer)`; `NewWithLevel`; `Records(t, buf) []Record`. |\n| `cmd/entire/main.go:17-52` | Load settings (graceful failure outside repo). Compute `level := logging.ResolveLevel(os.Getenv(logging.LogLevelEnvVar), s.LogLevel)`. Call `logger, closer := logging.New(ctx, logging.Options{Level: level})`. `ctx = logging.WithLogger(ctx, logger)`. `defer closer()`. Pass `ctx` to `rootCmd.ExecuteContext`. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go:60-89,97-121` | `initHookLogging` shrinks to: discover sessionID, return enriched ctx (`WithSession`). PreRunE: `cmd.SetContext(initHookLogging(cmd.Context()))`. **PersistentPostRunE deletes entirely.** Delete `hookLogCleanup` package var. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/attach.go:80`, `resume.go:74`, `clean.go:77`, `reset.go:32`, `rewind.go:71`, `explain.go:268`, `migrate.go:53` | **Delete** `logging.Init(ctx, \"\")` + `defer logging.Close()` + `logging.SetLogLevelGetter(GetLogLevel)`. Logger comes from `cmd.Context()` (already wired by main.go). For commands that need a session-scoped logger, wrap with `ctx = logging.WithSession(ctx, sid); cmd.SetContext(ctx)`. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/objectsigner.go` + `objectsigner_test.go` | **Delete both files** — dead duplicate of `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go` (commit `ddfbec1d2 Move checkpoint signer setup into CreateCommit`). Zero callers verified. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go` | Confirm signer path threads ctx everywhere it logs (current state already does). No changes expected; audit only. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go:389,616` | Add `ctx context.Context` param to `EnsureMetadataBranch` (line 389) and `decodeCheckpointInfo` (line 616). Replace `context.Background()` at lines 419, 648 with the threaded ctx. Update 4 internal callers. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/transcript.go:282` | Add `ctx` param to `extractTokenUsageFromEvents`. Replace `context.Background()` at line 292. Update single caller at line 276. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/agent/opencode/opencode.go:187` | Reshape `ReadSession` error handling to match other agents: don't log inside; return the `ExtractModifiedFiles` error or stash a warning on `*agent.AgentSession` for the caller to log. Drop the `context.Background()` log at line 200. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/config.go:74-83` | Drop `GetLogLevel` (or simplify to a thin wrapper around `settings.Load`). Drop the `//nolint:contextcheck` and the `context.TODO()`. |\n| `.golangci.yml` | Add `forbidigo` rule banning `logging\\.(Debug\\|Info\\|Warn\\|Error\\|LogDuration)\\(context\\.(Background\\|TODO)\\(\\)`. Future regressions caught at lint time. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed_tripwire_test.go:30`, `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/v2_committed_tripwire_test.go:25`, `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/hook_logging_test.go` | Replace `logging.Init`/`Close` with `loggingtest.New(t)` from new helper subpackage. |\n\n## Reused functions / utilities\n\n- `slog.With` from stdlib — does the heavy lifting; no custom attr-merging code needed.\n- `paths.WorktreeRoot(ctx)` — used inside `lazyWriter` on first write; preserves current behavior.\n- `redact.JSONLContent` — unchanged; logging output already passes through redaction at write time.\n\n## Migration order within the single PR (commit-by-commit suggested)\n\n1. **Add `loggingtest` subpackage.** No prod changes; helpers ready for later commits.\n2. **Add new `logging` API alongside old.** `New`, `WithLogger`, `LoggerFromContext`, `Closer`, `Options`, `ResolveLevel`, `lazyWriter`. Old `Init`/`Close`/`SetLogLevelGetter` still work. Compiles.\n3. **Wire `main.go` to `New` + `WithLogger`.** `ctx = logging.WithLogger(ctx, logger)`, `defer closer()`. Old `Init`/`Close` still run in commands; ctx-logger is dormant. Compiles.\n4. **Convert `WithSession`/`WithComponent`/`WithToolCall`/`WithAgent`/`WithParentSession` to enrich ctx-logger.** Drop public `*FromContext` getters (zero external callers). Keep private `sessionIDKey` for promotion. Compiles.\n5. **Flip `log()` to read from ctx.** Old `Init`-set globals become inert; ctx-logger is authoritative. Run full test suite.\n6. **Delete hook PostRunE + `hookLogCleanup`. Shrink hook PreRunE to `WithSession`.** Compiles.\n7. **Delete per-command Init/Close calls** (attach, resume, clean, reset, rewind, explain, migrate). Compiles.\n8. **Audit-fix `context.Background()` log sites:** `strategy/common.go` × 2, `agent/copilotcli/transcript.go`, `agent/opencode/opencode.go` (reshape error handling). Compiles.\n9. **Delete dead `cli/objectsigner.go` + test.** Compiles.\n10. **Delete obsolete logging globals + `Init`/`Close`/`SetLogLevelGetter`/`getLogger`/`getSessionID`/`attrsFromContext`.** Logging package is now globals-free.\n11. **Migrate test files** (`logger_test.go`, tripwire tests, integration tests) to `loggingtest.New(t)`. Add `t.Parallel()` everywhere in `logger_test.go`.\n12. **Add `forbidigo` rule** to `.golangci.yml`.\n\nEach commit compiles + tests pass. Reviewer can bisect if anything regresses.\n\n## Test strategy\n\n- Delete `resetLogger`. With no globals, every test is `t.Parallel()`-safe.\n- New helper subpackage `loggingtest` (~80 LOC):\n  ```go\n  func New(t testing.TB) (context.Context, *bytes.Buffer)\n  func NewWithLevel(t testing.TB, level slog.Level) (context.Context, *bytes.Buffer)\n  type Record struct {\n      Time time.Time; Level string; Msg string; Attrs map[string]any\n  }\n  func Records(t testing.TB, buf *bytes.Buffer) []Record\n  ```\n- `TestLogging_ConcurrentInitAndLog` becomes `TestLogging_ConcurrentLogToSharedLogger`: N goroutines log against the same ctx-logger; assert no data race under `-race` and N lines in buffer. Init-mid-write is no longer a scenario.\n- New tests in `logger_test.go`:\n  - `TestNew_LazyOpensFile`, `TestNew_FallsBackToStderrOnIOFailure` (sets unwritable dir).\n  - `TestNew_OutputOverridesLazyFile` (Options.Output != nil bypasses lazy logic).\n  - `TestLoggerFromContext_FallbackToDefault`.\n  - `TestWithSession_BakesAttr` (session_id appears in JSON output without `attrsFromContext`).\n  - `TestWithSession_PromotesParent` (existing → parent_session_id).\n  - `TestEnrichmentChain` (Session → Component → ToolCall composes correctly in output).\n  - `TestResolveLevel` (env wins, settings fallback, info default, invalid → info).\n  - `TestCloser_Idempotent` (calling closer twice doesn't error or double-close).\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- **Pre-`New` logging in main.go.** Anything before `New` returns uses `slog.Default()` (stderr text). main.go logs nothing this early; signal-handler errors use `fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, ...)` directly.\n- **Outside a git repo** (e.g. `entire --version`). `paths.WorktreeRoot` fails inside `lazyWriter`; one-shot warning + stderr fallback.\n- **`entire enable`** runs before `.entire/` exists. `lazyWriter` opens on first log call. If enable creates the directory before its first log, the file opens cleanly. Otherwise stderr fallback.\n- **`logging.X(context.Background(), ...)` after refactor** silently goes to `slog.Default()` (stderr). Behavior change: today such calls write to file via the global. Mitigation: forbidigo lint rule + Q7-D audit covers all 4 known live sites at refactor time. New regressions blocked at lint.\n- **Settings load failure in main.go** (outside repo, malformed file). main.go does `s, err := settings.Load(ctx); settingsLevel := \"\"; if err == nil { settingsLevel = s.LogLevel }`. Level falls through to env or `Info`.\n- **Cobra `cmd.SetContext`** propagates to subcommands via `cmd.Context()`. Verified pattern in current `hooks_git_cmd.go` flow.\n- **Test parallelism.** Add `t.Parallel()` to every test in `logger_test.go`. With no globals, race-free.\n- **Closer idempotency.** `sync.Once`-guarded inside `Closer`. main.go's defer is the only expected caller, but tests may close early.\n- **Hook `IsSetUpAndEnabled` gate.** Hook PreRunE still gates on `settings.IsSetUpAndEnabled(ctx)`; if false, just returns ctx unchanged — no enrichment, no error.\n\n## Verification\n\n1. `grep -rn \"logging\\.\\(Init\\|Close\\|SetLogLevelGetter\\)\" cmd/ e2e/` → zero hits.\n2. `grep -n \"var logger\\|var logFile\\|var logBufWriter\\|var currentSessionID\\|var mu \" cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go` → empty.\n3. `grep -rn \"hookLogCleanup\" cmd/` → empty.\n4. `grep -rn \"context\\.Background()\" cmd/entire/cli/objectsigner.go` → file gone.\n5. `grep -rn \"logging\\.\\(Debug\\|Info\\|Warn\\|Error\\|LogDuration\\)(context\\.\\(Background\\|TODO\\)\" cmd/ e2e/` → zero hits in production code.\n6. `mise run check` passes (fmt + lint + test:ci). `forbidigo` rule in `.golangci.yml` active.\n7. `go test -race -count=10 ./cmd/entire/cli/logging/...` clean — repeated to catch flaky races.\n8. `go test -race ./...` clean.\n9. `mise run test:e2e:canary` — full Vogon E2E suite passes (52 tests).\n10. Manual: run `entire hooks git post-commit` in a test repo, tail `.entire/logs/entire.log`, confirm `session_id`, `component`, `agent` appear on every line; `tool_call_id` only on tool-call lines.\n11. Manual: `entire --version` outside a repo — graceful stderr fallback, no `.entire/logs` created, no panic, no warning (lazy writer never opens).\n12. Manual: `pkill -INT entire` mid-hook — log file ends on a complete JSON line (closer flushed via signal handler reaching main.go's defer).\n13. Manual: induce log-file open failure (`chmod 000 .entire/logs/`) — confirm one-shot stderr warning, subsequent logs go to stderr, no panic.\n\n## Critical files\n\n- `/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go`\n- `/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/cli/logging/context.go`\n- `/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger_test.go`\n- `/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/cli/logging/loggingtest/loggingtest.go` (new)\n- `/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/main.go`\n- `/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go`\n- `/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/cli/objectsigner.go` (delete)\n- `/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/cli/objectsigner_test.go` (delete)\n- `/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go`\n- `/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/transcript.go`\n- `/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/add-auto-aupdate/cmd/entire/