{"parentUuid":"512eb204-c8ac-441b-b452-6046a049d09c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bfeff745-2b01-4c90-b4a7-e8ee245ef793","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012GvKPUBzhcAAEcE2hBfPWh","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"data\":{\"repository\":{\"pullRequest\":{\"reviewThreads\":{\"nodes\":[{\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOQyo98M5-MN_u\",\"isResolved\":false,\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/logging/context.go\",\"line\":33,\"comments\":{\"nodes\":[{\"databaseId\":3155534239,\"author\":{\"login\":\"cursor\"},\"body\":\"### Duplicate session_id JSON keys when sessions nest\\n\\n**Medium Severity**\\n\\n<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->\\n`WithSession` retrieves the ctx-carried logger (which already has `session_id` baked in from a prior `WithSession` call) and appends a new `session_id` attr via `slog.With`. Since `slog.With` appends without removing existing attrs, the resulting logger emits duplicate `session_id` JSON keys — e.g. `{\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"parent\\\",\\\"parent_session_id\\\":\\\"parent\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"child\\\",...}`. The old context-value approach rebuilt attrs from scratch on every log call, so duplicates never occurred. Most JSON parsers silently take the last value, which masks the issue, but duplicate keys violate RFC 7159's SHOULD-be-unique recommendation and can break log analysis tooling that uses a different strategy.\\n<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->\\n\\n<!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: 98f9389e-fc93-43cd-9077-b7e742584b76 -->\\n\\n<!-- LOCATIONS START\\ncmd/entire/cli/logging/context.go#L23-L33\\nLOCATIONS END -->\\n<div><a href=\\\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\\\"><img alt=\\\"Fix in Cursor\\\" width=\\\"115\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https://cursor.com/agents?REDACTED\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-light.png\\\"><img alt=\\\"Fix in Web\\\" width=\\\"99\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\\\"></picture></a></div>\\n\\n\\n<sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit c0d28e6a5575d4e396ae052024e83d727b919cb9. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-04-28T16:01:00Z\"}]}},{\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOQyo98M5-MN_y\",\"isResolved\":false,\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\".golangci.yaml\",\"line\":98,\"comments\":{\"nodes\":[{\"databaseId\":3155534246,\"author\":{\"login\":\"cursor\"},\"body\":\"### Forbidigo rule pattern cannot match call arguments\\n\\n**Low Severity**\\n\\n<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->\\nThe `forbidigo` pattern includes `\\\\(\\\\s*context\\\\.(Background|TODO)\\\\(\\\\)` to match arguments, but `forbidigo` matches patterns against the callee expression (e.g. `logging.Debug`), not the full call including arguments. Since the pattern requires `\\\\(` after the function name — which isn't part of the callee text — it will never match any expression. The lint guard advertised in the PR description to prevent future `logging.X(context.Background(), …)` regressions is therefore ineffective. It passed lint cleanly only because all violations were already removed.\\n<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->\\n\\n<!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: 49261fd1-e6d5-400a-bdba-d548b5c13025 -->\\n\\n<!-- LOCATIONS START\\n.golangci.yaml#L96-L98\\nLOCATIONS END -->\\n<div><a href=\\\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopene