Qyo98M5-MRgc\",\"isResolved\":false,\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/logging/context.go\",\"line\":32,\"comments\":{\"nodes\":[{\"databaseId\":3155554034,\"author\":{\"login\":\"copilot-pull-request-reviewer\"},\"body\":\"`WithSession` enriches the logger via `l.With(\\\"session_id\\\", ...)` even when the ctx already carries a logger that may already have a `session_id` attr. Calling `WithSession` multiple times (as supported by the parent-promotion logic) will accumulate duplicate JSON keys (e.g., multiple `session_id` fields) in the output, which can break strict JSON log consumers. To avoid duplicate keys, consider keeping these values in context and having `log()` append a de-duplicated attr set per call, or storing a base logger in context and rebuilding an enriched logger from that base each time.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-04-28T16:04:17Z\"}]}},{\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOQyo98M5-MRgw\",\"isResolved\":false,\"isOutdated\":true,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/opencode/opencode.go\",\"line\":null,\"comments\":{\"nodes\":[{\"databaseId\":3155554071,\"author\":{\"login\":\"copilot-pull-request-reviewer\"},\"body\":\"In `ReadSession`, the comment says the caller should decide how to surface non-fatal `ExtractModifiedFiles` errors, but the code discards the error entirely (`modifiedFiles, _ := ...`). That makes it impossible for callers to react (warn, metric, etc.). Either return a non-nil error (while still returning a usable session) or capture the non-fatal error in the returned `AgentSession` so the caller with a ctx can handle it.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-04-28T16:04:17Z\"}]}},{\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOQyo98M5-MRhC\",\"isResolved\":false,\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/logging/loggingtest/loggingtest.go\",\"line\":70,\"comments\":{\"nodes\":[{\"databaseId\":3155554093,\"author\":{\"login\":\"copilot-pull-request-reviewer\"},\"body\":\"`Records` iterates using `json.Decoder.More()`, which is only defined for parsing within an array/object. Since the lo